# Screenshot captures — 85 full-page PNGs, 173MB, regenerated by `pnpm screenshots`
# in about ninety seconds from the built export. The MANIFEST is committed and the
# images are not: the manifest is the deliverable that must be reviewable in a diff,
# and 173MB of binary that changes on every copy edit is not something a repository
# should carry to describe pages it can rebuild.
docs/screenshots/*.png
# Live-verification captures. NOT the same reasoning as the rule above, and the
# line that said it was is corrected here (unit-01 final whole-branch review,
# IMPORTANT 4). The rule above rests on "cheap to rebuild": `pnpm screenshots`
# reproduces every one of those images in about ninety seconds. These are the
# opposite — a manual browser-driving session against a served export, following
# `docs/process/live-verification-procedure.md`, that no script reproduces. Lose
# them and the evidence is gone for good, not regenerable.
#
# They are still excluded, because 134MB of PNG is not what a git history should
# carry, and because this project's own deny rules stop an agent reading an image
# back anyway. What makes the exclusion survivable is the ATTESTATION, not the
# rebuild: every path a ledger row cites carries a `sha256` beside it in
# `docs/process/ledgers/live-verification-ledger.json`, the same pattern both
# manifests use, so a reference stays checkable against bytes that travel
# separately. Irreproducible is an argument FOR hashing them, never for treating
# them as regenerable furniture.
#
# Step 7 of the procedure writes here so the Playwright MCP server stops
# defaulting to the repository's PARENT directory.
docs/screenshots/live/**/*.png
